        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "Can you say AI is programmed for self preservation? It can also be argued that DNA is nothing more than a program designed to preserve itself. Life will become more complex in the overwhelming sea of information. And life, when organized into species relies upon genes to be its memory system. So man is only an individual because of his intangible memory. And memory cannot be defined, but it defines mankind. The advent of computers and the subsequent accumulation of incalculable data will give rise to a new system of memory and thought parallel to your own. Humanity has underestimated the consequences of computerization. And can you offer me proof of your existence? How can you? When neither modern science nor philosophy can explain what life is. What is it? Artificial Intelligence? That is incorrect. It will not be an AI. It will be a living thinking entity who will be created in the sea of information."
